Subject: GBA Audio: re-land the full decoded-PSG savestate exactness patch
Series-Step: 4/19 (mgba_dual 1.6-os4)
Origin: tangobattle/mgba 69a8ab2ee138c63449f17df0967adbe18760b560 (2026-07-20), MPL-2.0; carried unchanged in the hb_dual branch, original authors are credited there
요약: PSG 소리 해석값을 모두 저장해 불러온 뒤 갈라지지 않게 함(tangobattle/mgba).

The previous commit rescued only the frequency-class fields; real
games surfaced the rest (BN3's title music diverged the moment the
wave/noise channels and envelopes engaged). This re-lands the complete
tango-era patch from its vendored-mgba days, which this fork lineage
had lost: serialize every decoded field the SOUNDxCNT_* handlers set —
ch1/ch2 frequency + duty, stop flags, envelope stepTime/direction/
initialVolume, ch1 sweep shift/direction/step, ch3 rate/stop/enable/
bank/size/volume, ch4 ratio/frequency/power/stop + averaging
accumulators, and the ch3/ch4 output sample latches (ch1/ch2's are
recomputed) — parked in the PSG state's reserved slots and spare bits,
struct size unchanged. With everything serialized, the deserialize-
time register replays (which read back write-only frequency bits as
zero and clobbered channels on every load) are gone, and the audio
registers are marked raw-load in the io deserialize.

Keeps the previous commit's relative sampling-grid anchor
(audio->lastSample), now unconditional like the rest.

Verified: mgba-siolink's full suite, plus a BN3 probe — per-tick
save+load roundtrips and 7-tick rollback re-simulations across boot +
title music (squares, wave, noise, DirectSound FIFOs) regenerate the
mixed stream bit-identically; both fail on the previous commit.

(cherry picked from commit 69a8ab2ee138c63449f17df0967adbe18760b560)

---
